    "Briefly, how do you perform a Principal Component Analysis? Should I get anxious about its mathematics?": "PCA reduces dimensions by transforming data into principal components (PCs), which are orthogonal axes capturing variance. Steps: center the data (subtract mean), compute covariance matrix, eigen-decompose it, and order eigenvalues descending. Math is manageable if you’re comfortable linear algebra—matrix operations and eigenvectors are systematic! Fear comes from complexity; breaking it into steps reduces anxiety.",
